  45: WDCS_DRQ|WDCI_IN so that arm is set too -- and ERR (0x01) only when d->error.
  46: wdc_command() assigns `d->error = 0` at its top, so after ATAPI_PKT_CMD the ERR
  47: bit is CLEAR.  Expected: 0x58.  (The wdcringambig probe sees 0x59 because it
  48: issues no command at all and the power-on d->error = 1 stands.)
  49: 
  50: WHY FREE-RUNNING AND NOT `step`:  DEVINIT sets d->data_debug = 1, so every
  51: data-port access calls debug().  debug() adds 1 to `verbose` when single_step is
  52: set and subtracts 1 when emul_executing, so a STEPPED run prints a line per
  53: access while a FREE-RUNNING run at default verbosity has v == -1 and prints
